<article class="env-remark" id="0F02">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0F02">Remark <span data-tag="0F02">59.88.1</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to S$ be a morphism of schemes. Let $n$ be an integer. We will say $BC(f, n, q_0)$ is true if for every commutative diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ X \ar[d]_ f &  X' \ar[l] \ar[d]_{f'} &  Y \ar[l]^ h \ar[d]^ e \\  S &  S' \ar[l] &  T \ar[l]_ g }  \]
</div>
  <p> with $X' = X \times _ S S'$ and $Y = X' \times _{S'} T$ and $g$ quasi-compact and quasi-separated, and every abelian sheaf $\mathcal{F}$ on $T_{\acute{e}tale}$ annihilated by $n$ the base change map </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  (f')^{-1}R^ qg_*\mathcal{F} \longrightarrow R^ qh_*e^{-1}\mathcal{F}  \]
</div>
  <p> is an isomorphism for $q \leq q_0$. </p>
</article>